  "notes": "Curriculum guide as printed in the 2023-2024 ASU Undergraduate Catalog (Dept. of English, Languages and Mass Communication). To enter the English Education program, students must pass PRAXIS Core Academic Skills for Educators and apply for admission to the teacher education program (44 semester hours, 2.75 GPA). Restricted courses (ED 302, ED 454, ED 248, ED 351, EN 485) require teacher education admission; ED 468 Directed Teaching requires passing Praxis II (5624 and 5038). All students must earn a C or above in each upper-level English course. *Restricted Course in School of Education. **Required Social Science courses in Education. ***Or other approved Creative Arts course.",
